<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.4 PCT IN NOV 1-20 -NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.4 PCT IN NOV 1-20 -NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 490</p>
<p>million zlotys, or 0.4 percent, in November 1-20 to 126.47</p>
<p>billion after a 2.2 percent rise in all of October, National</p>
<p>Bank of Poland (NBP) preliminary figures showed.</p>
<p>BROAD POLISH MONEY		  NOV 1-20    OCTOBER	NOV 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	    0.4	2.2		2.2</p>
<p> Money in bln zlotys		 126.47   125.98(126.04)  99.62</p>
<p> Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    22.85    22.52 (22.51)  20.94</p>
<p> National currency		   103.64   103.46(103.53)  78.68</p>
<p> Cash in circulation		  22.85    23.49 (23.51)  19.14</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial sector  75.70    73.45 (73.41)  55.38</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
